{
  "title": "India says new IT fact-checking unit will not censor journalism",
  "publication_date": "2023-04-14T00:00:00Z",
  "summary": "India's government clarified that its proposed fact-checking unit for social media news will not censor journalism or affect media reporting, according to a federal minister's statement.",
  "content": "NEW DELHI, April 14 (Reuters) - A proposed Indian government unit to fact-check news on social media is not about censoring journalism nor will it have any impact on media reportage, a federal minister said on Friday.\n\nRecently amended IT regulations require social media companies to take down content that a government-appointed fact-checking unit identifies as \"fake or false.\" The move has sparked concerns about state censorship among journalists and media organizations.\n\nThe government maintains that the fact-checking unit is necessary to combat the spread of misinformation on social media platforms while preserving press freedom.",
