  "markdown_content": "## Government Response to Fact-Checking Concerns\\n\\nNEW DELHI, April 14 (Reuters) - A proposed Indian government unit to fact-check news on social media \"is not about censoring journalism nor will it have any impact on media reportage,\" a federal minister said on Friday.\\n\\nRecently amended IT regulations require social media companies to take down content that a government-appointed fact-checking unit identifies as \"fake or false.\" The move has sparked concerns about state censorship among journalists and media organizations.\\n\\nThe government maintains that the fact-checking unit is necessary to combat the spread of misinformation on social media platforms while preserving press freedom.",
